course: dictionary
lesson: 3725
title: Flint: a hard stone with a spark
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Flint is a noun, a word for a thing. A flint is a very hard grey or black stone. You can find out a lot about it from the words around it. «Striking steel on flint knocks off tiny bits of steel made so hot by the blow that they burn as sparks; people lit fires this way long ago.» The sentence tells you that flint and steel together make sparks, and that people used this long ago to start fires.
explain: Flint breaks into sharp edges, and people used those edges. In history lessons on the Stone Age, people made axes, knives and arrowheads from flint. Ask yourself: what would a sharp stone be good for? A flint knife cuts, and a flint arrowhead can be fixed to a stick.
explain: Some words are not about stones at all. In a story, a «heart of flint» means a very hard, unkind heart. The stone is hard, so the word describes a person who will not bend or show kindness. This is a picture word, and the clue is in the stone itself.
fact: Flint is a very hard grey or black stone.
fact: Flint makes sparks when it is struck against steel.
fact: Flint breaks into sharp edges, so people made tools and arrowheads from it.
fact: Flint is found in chalk, for example on beaches and cliffs in southern England.
fact: A «heart of flint» means a very hard, unkind heart.
exercise: «Striking steel on flint knocks off tiny bits of steel made so hot by the blow that they burn as sparks.» What makes the sparks? | Water poured on the stone | Chalk crumbling away | Wind blowing over the sea | *Tiny bits of steel knocked off and burning
exercise: In a story, someone has «a heart of flint». What does this mean? | A heart made of metal that beats loudly | *A very hard, unkind heart | A kind and gentle heart | A heart that is full of light
exercise: Where in southern England can you find flint? | On the tops of tall trees | *On beaches and cliffs in chalk | Deep inside the Scottish mountains | Inside a lighter's flame
test: What did people long ago use flint for? | Painting pictures on cave walls | *Making arrowheads and lighting fires | Making glass windows | Making sweets and cakes
test: «Tegumai's eyes shine: he thinks his daughter has found the biggest secret of the world.» What does Tegumai think his daughter has found? | *The biggest secret of the world | A new kind of fire | Some shark's teeth | A pile of flints for trading
exam: What is flint, and what does it do when it is struck against steel? | A wooden stick that bursts into flames | *A very hard grey or black stone that makes sparks | A metal that bends easily and glows red | A soft white stone that melts in water
